&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Joining Collibra’s Growth Marketing team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Collibra&#39;s Growth Marketing team drives the regional strategies and programs that connect our solutions to the accounts and buyers who need them most — and we&#39;re looking for an EMEA Senior Field Marketing Manager to lead that charge across the region. Reporting to the Director of Field &amp;amp; Event Marketing, you&#39;ll own the strategy and execution that influences the pipeline across EMEA from building awareness with the right accounts to accelerating opportunities through demand generation and targeted account-based plays.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll partner closely with EMEA GTM leaders, Integrated Marketing, and Growth Marketing to translate global programs into high-impact regional initiatives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Values-in-action (We show up to win): This team moves with urgency, makes data-driven decisions, and continuously optimizes to deliver the best outcomes for the business and our customers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hybrid role based in our London office. Our hybrid model means you’ll work from the office at least two days each week. This setup helps us stay connected, work more closely together, and keep making progress as a team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Senior Field Marketing Managers at Collibra are responsible for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and execute fully integrated, multi-channel marketing plans across the UKI, ME and Southern Europe regions to drive demand generation, land new logos, and achieve new business pipeline targets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and run Account-Based Marketing (ABM) programs in close partnership with sales — identifying and prioritizing high-value accounts, personalizing engagement across channels, and accelerating pipeline progression within target accounts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate global campaigns into regional digital and engagement roadmaps, providing strategic direction based on EMEA industry frameworks and market dynamics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Align with GTM leaders, Integrated Marketing, and Growth Marketing to develop EMEA field marketing priorities and multi-channel plans using a data-driven approach to decision making&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor and analyze marketing performance, delivering insights that optimize strategies and investments to maximize ROI against revenue objectives&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of experience in Field, Partner, or Channel Marketing in a B2B enterprise technology environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record delivering regional demand generation programs that achieve pipeline targets, with measurable results across top, mid, and bottom of funnel&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing and executing ABM programs, including partnering with sales to define target account lists and drive personalized engagement at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cross-functional program management experience executing integrated marketing programs, including with enterprise partners such as SAP, Google Cloud, or GSIs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills, with experience presenting marketing strategy and performance to senior stakeholders and customer audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Candidates proficiency in French preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to travel up to 25%&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated proficiency in leveraging AI tools (e.g., Claude, Gemini, ChatGPT, Copilot) to solve real-world business challenges, drive measurable outcomes, or streamline workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A bachelor’s degree or equivalent related working experience is required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Metrics-driven and analytical you translate data into clear insights and use them to make fast, informed investment decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborative and skilled at building alignment across GTM, sales, and marketing to move programs forward with shared accountability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactive and solutions-oriented, anticipating obstacles and operating with urgency in a fast-paced, high-growth environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiar with applying marketing technologies including Salesforce, Tableau, 6Sense, HockeyStack, Asana, and event platforms such as Zuddl&amp;nbsp; to manage programs and measure results&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Adaptable and comfortable navigating ambiguity, iterating quickly based on market feedback and performance data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent in English&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Measures of success&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Within your first month, you will: Complete onboarding, build key relationships with EMEA GTM leaders and cross-functional marketing partners, and conduct an audit of current EMEA field marketing programs and pipeline performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Within your third month, you will: Own and execute your first regional marketing program, partner with sales to define and align on the ABM target account strategy, and begin contributing measurably to the EMEA pipeline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Within your sixth month, you will: Deliver measurable progress against EMEA pipeline targets, maintain a full regional marketing calendar, and demonstrate ABM-driven improvements in target account engagement and pipeline progression.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;Benefits at Collibra&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Collibra recognizes and values that everyone has different needs, interests, and life goals. We built our benefits program with flexibility in mind to support you and your loved ones through a diverse range of circumstances and life events. These flexible offerings sit on a foundation of competitive compensation, health coverage, and time off. Learn more about &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.collibra.com/us/en/company/careers/benefits&quot;&gt;Collibra’s benefits&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We create inclusion and belonging through how we onboard, meet, connect, engage, and communicate. Learn more about&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.collibra.com/us/en/company/careers/dei&quot;&gt;diversity, equity, and inclusion&lt;/a&gt; at Collibra.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Collibra, we’re proud to be an equal opportunity employer. We realize the key to creating a company with a world-class culture and employee experience comes from who we hire and creating a workplace that celebrates everyone.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With this, we proudly consider qualified applicants without regard to race, color, religion, creed, gender, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, pregnancy, sex, gender identity, gender expression, genetic information, physical or mental disability, HIV status, registered domestic partner status, caregiver status, marital status, veteran or military status, citizenship status or any other legally protected category. If you have a need that requires accommodation, let us know by completing our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.collibra.com/us/en/company/careers/accommodations&quot;&gt;Accommodations for Applicants form&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

66804fc6b6bfff52.description:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Sony Interactive Entertainment?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Sony Interactive Entertainment isn’t just the Best Place to Play — it’s also the Best Place to Work. Sony Interactive Entertainment (SIE) is the company behind the PlayStation brand. As a subsidiary of Sony Group Corporation, we’re part of a proud legacy of innovation and excellence. SIE is a dynamic technology company, delivering cutting-edge hardware and network services to more than 100 million people and an entertainment leader, home to some of the most beloved and recognizable intellectual properties (IP) in the world. Our role at SIE is to create and nurture the experiences under the PlayStation brand, a name synonymous with entertainment excellence and creativity.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Competitive Analysis &amp;amp; Insights function is part of the Platform &amp;amp; Business Analytics department in Sony Interactive Entertainment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SIE creates extraordinary experiences around play that inspire millions of people to interact with our products and services. Our team supports global product and business partners by developing actionable competitive insights providing essential context to inform strategic decision making.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Senior Analyst is responsible for driving and completing competitive analysis projects. They need to be self-motivated and independent, capable of managing multiple projects from start to finish, working with varied sets of product &amp;amp; business partners. Their role is crucial in enhancing our analytical capabilities, output, and influence to inform the successful development, market launch, and operation of SIE products. Working alongside the existing team, their role will combine qualitative judgment with strengthening and elevating the team’s quantitative analysis capabilities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll be doing:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Crafting and delivering impactful, actionable competitive market analyses and insights using all relevant sources and employing qualitative and quantitative methods&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contributing to and developing our competitive analysis methodology as this function evolves within SIE, with a focus on quantitative analysis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assess market developments, competitor performance and platform strategies using relevant data paired with qualitative insight&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Managing analysis projects end-to-end, from initial briefing through to final delivery, follow-up, and impact assessment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Developing repeatable analytical workflows and models that combine and validate internal &amp;amp; external data, critically assess evidence, and size markets and opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Managing and developing intelligence assets, including sourcing, processing, aggregating data, providing access, and distributing information&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serving as the point of contact and representative for our team within the broader organisation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improving research efficiency through responsible adoption and implementation of AI tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we are looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re a highly capable market analyst with strongly developed skills in competitive and market analysis and relevant experience in the gaming industry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re passionate about the gaming sector and knowledgeable about the PC and Mobile categories, and the latest advancements in technology relevant to gaming&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re a self-starter who can handle high-level project briefs with varying ambiguity and develop, manage and deliver multiple analysis projects in parallel&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re an excellent communicator, crafting compelling narratives and effectively interacting with and influencing diverse stakeholders across all levels of the organisation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re a strategic thinker with the ability to translate research into plausible scenarios and business implications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You excel in quantitative and qualitative analysis and pragmatically adapt your approach to anticipate, interpret and meet client needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have practical SQL proficiency at extracting and combining data, together with strong spreadsheet modelling skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re able to assess source and data quality, reconcile conflicting evidence and explain uncertainty clearly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You take ownership of project success, leading with passion and investment, and are proactive and hands-on when required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You value and contribute to a diverse team and foster a culture of transparency, curiosity, constructive problem-solving, relationship building and continuous improvement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience as a senior analyst in the games industry with a strong understanding of the gaming business and its main actors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of success in delivering impactful competitive analyses &amp;amp; insight&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in primary and secondary source research, data management and manipulation using relevant tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent storytelling and presentation abilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong project management skills to dependably deliver end-to-end projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Desirable&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience within a product-related function&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience engaging with Senior Executives and diverse stakeholder sets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with market insight and consultancy firms and familiarity with gaming market datasets and their coverage, methodologies and limitations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing scenario frameworks, competitor response assessments or indicators for ongoing monitoring&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in written and spoken Japanese would be highly advantageous, though not required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;Please note, Sony Interactive Entertainment conducts background checks at the offer stage for all new employees (which may include criminal background checks for some roles) and will need to process personal information to support these checks.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;Please refer to our Candidate Privacy Notice (where applicable) for more information about what personal information we collect, how we use it, who we share it with, and your data protection rights.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal Opportunity Statement:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Sony is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All persons will receive consideration for employment without regard to gender (including gender identity, gender expression and gender reassignment), race (including colour, nationality, ethnic or national origin), religion or belief, marital or civil partnership status, disability, age, sexual orientation, pregnancy, maternity or parental status, trade union membership or membership in any other legally protected category.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
